---
/*
  FontLoader.astro
  Both font stylesheets are imported with ?url so Vite emits them (and the
  woff2 files they reference) as standalone hashed assets instead of inlining
  the @font-face declarations into every page's CSS bundle. font-preload.mjs
  injects per-page <link rel="preload"> for the LXGW subsets each page uses.

  Render-blocking on purpose. The webfonts are font-display: optional, so a
  stylesheet that lands after first paint never swaps glyphs in mid-view —
  repeat visits would lose their cached fonts instead of gaining them.
  Blocking puts the @font-face rules (and the cached woff2 files) inside
  optional's 100 ms block window, so repeat views paint with the real fonts
  on the first frame while cold visits render the fallback with no swap.
  Both files are immutable-cached /_astro assets, so the blocking cost is
  paid once per cache, not per navigation.
*/
import lxgwCss from "lxgw-wenkai-webfont/lxgwwenkai-regular.css?url";
import jbmonoCss from "../styles/fonts.css?url";
---

<link rel="stylesheet" href={lxgwCss} />
<link rel="stylesheet" href={jbmonoCss} />
